1. SETUP AND RUN INSTRUCTIONS

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Prerequisites: .NET 8.0 SDK installed.



Commands:

• Restore Dependencies:

  dotnet restore



• Start Application:

  dotnet run --project CourseWaitlist.Api --urls "http://localhost:5000"



• Access Swagger UI:

  Open http://localhost:5000/swagger in browser.



• Run Automated Unit & Concurrency Tests:

  dotnet test



--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. LIMITATIONS & SCOPE RISKS

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• In-Memory Volatility: State resets on server restart as data is stored in-memory

  rather than a persistent database.

• Single-Instance Concurrency: Thread safety is enforced via SemaphoreSlim, 

  which works for a single process but would require distributed locking 

  (e.g., Redis) if scaled across multiple instances.

• Unauthenticated Endpoints: Endpoints take raw `learnerId` without authentication,

  which would require JWT authorization in a production environment.

• Single Course Focus: Optimized for a single course offering (`CS101`) for 

  prototype evaluation rather than multi-course relational scheduling.



